{% extends '@CitadelAureum/core/docs/layout.html.twig' %}

{% block article %}
    <p>
        Fines records chargeable incidents (damage, smoking, missed
        cancellations) with a clear paper trail from the incident to its
        resolution, including any appeal the guest raises.
    </p>

    <h2>How a fine moves</h2>
    <p>
        A fine starts as <strong>not appealed</strong>. If the guest disputes it,
        record the appeal as <strong>appeal submitted</strong>, and once a
        decision is made, <strong>appeal completed</strong>. Every change is
        kept in the fine's log.
    </p>

    <h2>Common tasks</h2>
    <ol class="au-docs-steps">
        <li>Open <strong>General → Fines</strong> to see recorded fines.</li>
        <li>Record a fine promptly with the incident details and amount. Accuracy matters if it's appealed later.</li>
        <li>With manage permission, update the status as the appeal progresses.</li>
    </ol>
{% endblock %}
